.TH CGFRIED 1 "2026-10-12" "Cgfried 0.1.0" "Cgfried Manual"
.SH NAME
cgfried, cgf \- deterministic C17 compiler for five explicit targets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgfried
.RI [ options ] " file" ...
.br
.B cgf
.RI [ options ] " file" ...
.br
.B cgfried
.RI [ options ]
.BR \-E | \-S | \-c
.RI [ \-o " output" ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgfried
is a self-hosting C compiler with x86-64 and ARM64 backends.  It emits ELF or
Mach-O for a closed set of five targets, supplies freestanding headers and
.BR libcgf_rt ,
and drives either system tools or the companion
.B afs-as
and
.B afs-ld
tools.
.PP
The default language mode is ISO C17.  The accepted
.B \-std=
modes are c89, c90, c99, c11, c17, c18, their iso9899 aliases, and the
corresponding GNU modes.  Unlike GCC, the default does not enable GNU
extensions.
.PP
Version 0.1.0 is intentionally bounded.  It is not a drop-in GCC replacement.
C23, _Complex, threads.h, general-dynamic TLS, full DWARF, LTO, PGO, and
asm goto are outside this release and are rejected rather than silently
miscompiled.  Applicable unsupported standard facilities are advertised with
the corresponding __STDC_NO_* feature macros.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Information and target selection
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help=warnings
Print every warning option and its current default/group state.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the frozen three-line release identity and license notice.
.TP
.B \-dumpversion
Print the full semantic version and a newline.
.TP
.B \-dumpmachine
Print the exact selected target spelling and a newline.
.TP
.B \-print\-search\-dirs
Print the compiler's resolved program and library search directories.
.TP
.BI \-print\-prog\-name= program
Print the resolved path of a tool, or the supplied name when unresolved.
.TP
.BI \-print\-file\-name= file
Print the first resolved library/start-file path, or the supplied name.
.TP
.BI \-\-target= triple
Select exactly one of x86_64-linux-gnu, arm64-linux, arm64-macos,
x86_64-linux-musl, or x86_64-freebsd.
.TP
.BI \-arch " arm64"
Require the arm64-macos target for Apple build-system compatibility.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot= directory
Resolve target headers, libraries, and start files beneath
.IR directory .
.TP
.B \-m64
Require an x86-64 target and its 64-bit ABI.
.TP
.B \-v
Print each external command before it runs.
.TP
.B \-###
Analyze inputs and print the exact command plan without running external
commands.
.SS Compilation modes and output
.TP
.B \-E
Preprocess only; write to standard output unless
.B \-o
is present.
.TP
.B \-S
Stop after assembly generation.
.TP
.B \-c
Compile and assemble without linking.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Name the output.  It is invalid with multiple inputs under
.BR \-E ,
.BR \-S ,
or
.BR \-c .
.TP
.BI \-x " language"
Treat following inputs as
.B c
or
.BR none ;
a standard-input source requires
.BR "\-x c" .
.TP
.B \-P
Omit linemarkers from preprocessor output.
.TP
.B \-dM
With
.BR \-E ,
dump macro definitions.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
Dump preprocessing tokens for compiler development.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Dump the parsed syntax tree.
.TP
.B \-fdump\-sema
Dump semantic-analysis state.
.TP
.B \-fdump\-layout
Dump target record layouts.
.TP
.B \-fdump\-init
Dump lowered initializer data.
.TP
.B \-fsyntax\-only
Parse and analyze without producing output.
.TP
.B \-emit\-ir
Write deterministic textual Cgfried IR.
.TP
.B \-emit\-mir
Write target machine IR.
.SS Language and preprocessing
.TP
.BI \-std= standard
Select an ISO or GNU C language mode.  The last occurrence wins.
.TP
.B \-trigraphs
Enable trigraph translation.
.TP
.B \-pthread
Define _REENTRANT and add the target thread library at link time.
.TP
.B \-pedantic
Enable ISO conformance diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-pedantic\-errors
Promote ISO conformance diagnostics to errors.
.TP
.BI \-fmax\-errors= count
Stop after
.I count
errors; zero means unlimited.
.TP
.BI \-ferror\-limit= count
Alias for
.BR \-fmax\-errors= .
.TP
.BI \-I directory
Add a quote and angle include directory.
.TP
.BI \-iquote directory
Add a quote-only include directory.
.TP
.BI \-isystem directory
Add a system include directory after
.B \-I
directories and before built-in paths.
.TP
.BI \-include file
Include
.I file
before the first line of every C input.
.TP
.BI \-D "name[=value]"
Define a preprocessor macro; the omitted value is 1.
.TP
.BI \-U name
Undefine a preprocessor macro.  Definitions and undefinitions are processed
in command-line order.
.TP
.B \-nostdinc
Do not search target system include directories.
.SS Dependency generation
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-MM
Write make dependencies to standard output and imply preprocessing;
.B \-MM
omits system headers.
.TP
.BR \-MD ", " \-MMD
Write a side-effect dependency file while compiling;
.B \-MMD
omits system headers.
.TP
.BI \-MF file
Set the dependency-file name.
.TP
.BI \-MT target
Add a dependency target verbatim.
.TP
.BI \-MQ target
Add a dependency target with make metacharacters quoted.
.TP
.B \-MP
Emit a phony target for every dependency header.
.SS Optimization, diagnostics, and safety
.TP
.BI \-O level
Select 0, 1, 2, 3, s, or fast.
.B \-O
alone means
.BR \-O1 ;
the last optimization option wins.
.TP
.B \-ftime\-report
Print per-pass invocation counts and wall time.
.TP
.B \-w
Suppress all warnings.
.TP
.B \-Werror
Promote all enabled warnings to errors.
.TP
.BI \-Werror= name
Promote one warning to an error.
.TP
.BI \-W name
Enable a warning or warning group.  Every positive spelling accepts the
.B \-Wno\-
form.  Exact options outrank groups regardless of argument order.
.TP
.BR \-Wall ", " \-Wextra ", " \-Wunused ", " \-Wformat ", " \-Wimplicit
Enable the named GCC-compatible warning groups.
.TP
.BR \-Wpedantic ", " \-Wcgf\-ext ", " \-Wmem ", " \-Wmem\-strict
Enable pedantic, Cgfried-extension, memory, or strict heuristic memory
diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-fcommon
Place tentative definitions in COMMON storage.
.TP
.B \-fno\-common
Emit one definition for tentative definitions; this is the default.
.TP
.B \-ffreestanding
Select a freestanding implementation.
.TP
.B \-fhosted
Restore hosted behavior.
.TP
.B \-fwrapv
Define signed overflow to wrap.
.TP
.B \-fgnu89\-inline
Use GNU89 inline-emission semantics.
.TP
.B \-fno\-gnu89\-inline
Use ISO inline-emission semantics.
.TP
.BR \-fstrict\-aliasing ", " \-fno\-strict\-aliasing
Enable or disable type-based alias analysis.
.TP
.BR \-fomit\-frame\-pointer ", " \-fno\-omit\-frame\-pointer
Control frame-pointer retention.
.TP
.B \-fcgf\-safe
Instrument unresolved heap accesses after static proof.
.TP
.B \-fno\-cgf\-safe
Disable heap instrumentation.
.TP
.B \-fsafe
Enable the safe-translation-unit policy: heap instrumentation, memory and
uninitialized warnings as errors, zero initialization, and unsafe-construct
rejection.
.TP
.BI \-fsafe\-allow\-unsafe= object
Permit exactly one explicitly linked unmarked object in a safe link.
.TP
.B \-fdiagnostics\-parseable\-fixits
Emit machine-readable fix-it records.
.TP
.B \-fdiagnostics\-apply\-fixits
Apply all safe edits to a
.B .cgf-fixed
copy; never rewrite the source.
.TP
.BI \-fdiagnostics\-apply\-fixits= mode
Select
.B all
or
.B interactive
fix-it application.
.TP
.B \-ftrivial\-auto\-var\-init
Initialize otherwise-uninitialized automatic objects with zero.
.TP
.BI \-ftrivial\-auto\-var\-init= mode
Select
.B zero
or
.B pattern
initialization.
.TP
.B \-ffast\-math
Enable Cgfried's complete fast-math bundle.
.TP
.B \-fno\-fast\-math
Disable the bundle.
.TP
.BR \-fassociative\-math ", " \-fno\-associative\-math
Accepted bundle-component controls; inconsistent standalone use warns.
.TP
.BR \-fsigned\-zeros ", " \-fno\-signed\-zeros
Accepted bundle-component controls for signed-zero assumptions.
.TP
.BR \-ffinite\-math\-only ", " \-fno\-finite\-math\-only
Accepted bundle-component controls for finite-value assumptions.
.TP
.BR \-freciprocal\-math ", " \-fno\-reciprocal\-math
Accepted bundle-component controls for reciprocal transforms.
.TP
.BR \-fmath\-errno ", " \-fno\-math\-errno
Accepted bundle-component controls for math errno behavior.
.TP
.BI \-ffp\-contract= mode
Select
.BR off ,
.BR on ,
or
.B fast
floating-point contraction.
.TP
.BI \-f option
Unknown
.B \-f
options warn and compilation continues for configure-script compatibility.
.TP
.BI \-g level
Emit DWARF v4 line information; levels 1, 2, and 3 currently have the same
line-table scope, and
.B \-g0
disables it.
.SS Linker and tool routing
.TP
.BI \-L directory
Add a library search directory.
.TP
.BI \-l library
Link a library at its command-line position.
.TP
.BI \-framework framework
Link an Apple framework on arm64-macos.
.TP
.BI \-Wl, argument
Pass comma-separated arguments to the linker in position.
.TP
.BI \-Xlinker argument
Pass one argument to the linker in position.
.TP
.BI \-B directory
Add a tool and start-file search prefix.
.TP
.B \-static
Request a static link.  arm64-macos rejects static linking.
.TP
.B \-shared
Request a shared link on supported target tiers.
.TP
.BR \-pie ", " \-no\-pie
Request or suppress a position-independent executable.
.TP
.B \-nostdlib
Omit start files and default libraries.
.TP
.B \-nostartfiles
Omit target start files.
.TP
.B \-nodefaultlibs
Omit default target libraries.
