.SH ENVIRONMENT
An empty value is treated as unset unless noted otherwise.
.TP
.B CGF_AS
Unset or 1 selects bundled afs-as; 0 selects the system assembler.
.TP
.B CGF_AS_PATH
Use exactly this assembler, overriding
.BR CGF_AS .
.TP
.B CGF_LD
Unset or 0 selects the system linker; 1 selects bundled afs-ld.
.TP
.B CGF_LD_PATH
Use exactly this linker, overriding
.BR CGF_LD .
.TP
.B CGF_CRT_DIR
Override target start-file discovery.
.TP
.B CGF_INCLUDE_DIR
Override the shipped freestanding-header directory.
.TP
.B CGF_SDKROOT
Override macOS SDK discovery.  A bad explicit path fails closed.
.TP
.B CGF_LIBSYSTEM_TBD
Override the macOS libSystem text-stub path.
.TP
.B CGF_STATS
When 1, print deterministic compiler allocation/interner/preprocessor counts.
.TP
.B CGF_MEMSAFE_DUMP
When 1, print memory-analysis states, traces, and discharged-check totals.
.TP
.B CGF_SAFE_ABORT
Set to
.B trap
to trap instead of aborting after a safe-runtime finding.
.TP
.B CGF_VERIFY_AFTER_EACH
When 1, verify IR after every optimization pass.
.TP
.B CGF_OPT_BAIL_LOG
When 1, report conservative optimizer bailouts.
.TP
.BR CGF_OPT_DISABLE_UNSWITCH ", " CGF_OPT_DISABLE_BCE ", " CGF_OPT_DISABLE_FUSION ", " CGF_OPT_DISABLE_VECTORIZE
When 1, disable the named optimization for differential testing.
.TP
.B CGF_DUMP_IR
Set to
.B all
to write every optimization phase.
.TP
.B CGF_DUMP_IR_DIR
Name the fresh, isolated directory required by
.BR CGF_DUMP_IR=all .
.TP
.B CGF_DUMP_BAD_IR
Name the file used to capture invalid IR at an internal-error boundary.
.TP
.BR CGF_PP_DUMP_TOKENS ", " CGF_PP_DUMP_GUARD
Enable preprocessor token or include-guard diagnostic dumps.
.TP
.BR CGF_PP_GUARD_FASTPATH ", " CGF_PP_STATS
Control the guarded-header fast path or preprocessor counters.
.TP
.B CGF_SPILL_ALL
Force register-allocation spill stress.
.TP
.B CGF_DIAG_FULL_BACKTRACE
Print the full macro-expansion diagnostic backtrace.
.TP
.B CGF_FUZZ
Enable bounded diagnostics suitable for the in-tree fuzz harnesses.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Decimal Unix timestamp used in UTC for __DATE__, __TIME__, the
.B \-\-version
copyright year, and reproducible release archives.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any nonempty value disables diagnostic color.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
Any nonempty value forces diagnostic color when
.B NO_COLOR
is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Compilation, option, preprocessing, parsing, semantic, or assembly-input
error.
.TP
.B 2
Linker or link-planning error.
.TP
.B 3
Input/output or tool-spawn error.
.TP
.B 4
Internal compiler error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile and link one translation unit with system tools:
.PP
.nf
CGF_AS=0 cgfried hello.c \-o hello
.fi
.PP
Compile and link multiple translation units:
.PP
.nf
CGF_AS=0 cgfried \-c one.c two.c
CGF_AS=0 cgfried one.o two.o \-o program
.fi
.PP
Preprocess without linemarkers:
.PP
.nf
cgfried \-E \-P config.h
.fi
.PP
Emit ARM64 Linux assembly:
.PP
.nf
cgfried \-\-target=arm64-linux \-S hello.c \-o hello.s
.fi
.PP
Compile a safe translation unit:
.PP
.nf
CGF_AS=0 cgfried \-fsafe app.c \-o app
.fi
.SH NOTES
Unlike historical GCC releases that print only the major component,
.B \-dumpversion
prints the full semantic version.  This is a frozen Cgfried build-system
contract from 0.1.0 onward.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gcc (1),
.BR as (1),
.BR ld (1)
.PP
The companion afs-as and afs-ld documentation is distributed in their
respective source subdirectories.  Cgfried's safe-mode and performance
contracts are in
.B doc/safe-mode.md
and
.BR doc/perf-gates.md .
